cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "The structure of A-free measures: a Lean 4 formalization of De Philippis and Rindler"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/scottnarmstrong/A-free-measures"
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked Lean 4 and Mathlib formalization of G. De Philippis and
  F. Rindler, On the structure of A-free measures and applications (Ann. of
  Math. 2016). Every theorem, lemma and corollary of the paper is formalized
  and proved, with Remarks 1.3, 1.4 and 1.11: the main theorem, that the
  polar of an A-free measure lies in the wave cone of A at almost every point
  of the singular part, for operators of every order, with
  a measure on the right-hand side and with variable coefficients; Alberti's
  rank-one theorem and its versions for higher derivatives and for BD
  functions; the structure of normal currents; the converse of Rademacher's
  theorem; and the absolute continuity of top-dimensional metric currents.
  The results of Alberti-Marchese and Ambrosio-Kirchheim that the proofs use
  are proved too. The library contains no sorry and no custom axiom.
authors:
  - family-names: Armstrong
    given-names: Scott
keywords:
  - Lean
  - mathlib
  - formal verification
  - geometric measure theory
  - A-free measures
  - normal currents
  - Rademacher theorem
license: Apache-2.0
